    <statement><tabular valign="top">
<row>
<cell>A bead is made from material with constant density
4 grams per cubic millimeter 
by drilling a cylindrical hole
of radius 2 mm through a sphere of radius 
6 mm.
(a) Set up a triple integral in cylindrical 
coordinates representing the mass of the
bead in grams (do not include units).  If necessary,
enter <m>\theta</m> as <em>theta.</em>
<CENTER><m>\displaystyle \iiint\limits_{Bead} f \, dV
=
\int_A^B \!\! \int_C^D \!\! \int_E^F \!\!</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>dz \, dr \, d\theta</m></CENTER>
A = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/>
B = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/>
C = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/>
D = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/>
E = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/>
F = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0007"/>
(b) Find the mass of the bead.
<p><fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0008"/> grams</p></cell>
